  "title": "77: al-Mursalaat المرسلات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالْمُرْسَلٰتِ عُرْفًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAL MURSALAATE U’URFAN.\nBy those sent forth with goodness, one after another\nفَالْعٰصِفٰتِ عَصْفًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL A’AASEFAATE A’ASFAN.\nWhich then rage in violent rage\nوَّالنّٰشِرٰتِ نَشْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nWWAALNNAASHERAATE NASHRAN.\nAnd by those which spread (goodness) far and wide\nفَالْفٰرِقٰتِ فَرْقًا ۙ‏(4)\nFAL FAAREQAATE FARQAN.\nThen by those that separate them from one another\nفَالْمُلْقِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(5)\nFAL MULQEETE ZIKRAA.\nThen by those that give forth the Reminder\nعُذْرًا اَوْ نُذْرًا ۙ‏(6)\nU’UZRAN AW NUZRAN.\nEither justify (the punishment), or to warn\nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(7)\nINNAMAA TOO-A’DOON LAWAAQEA’UN.\nVerily, what hath been promised unto you shall come to pass\nفَاِذَا النُّجُوْمُ طُمِسَتْۙ‏(8)\nFA-EZAA NOJOOMUN TUMESAT.\nSo, when the stars shall be caused to cease radiating\nوَ اِذَا السَّمَآءُ فُرِجَتْۙ‏(9)\nWA EZAA SAMAAA-O FUREJAT.\nAnd when the heaven shall be rent asunder\nوَاِذَا الْجِبَالُ نُسِفَتْۙ‏(10)\nWA EZAA JEBAALO NUSEFAT.\nAnd when the mountains shall be carried away like the dust\nوَاِذَا الرُّسُلُ اُقِّتَتْؕ‏(11)\nWA EZAA ROSOLO AUQQETAT.\nAnd when the messengers are made to reach their appointed time\nلِاَىِّ يَوْمٍ اُجِّلَتْؕ‏(12)\nLE-AYYE YAWMIN AUJJELAT.\nTo what day is the appointment (fixed)?\nلِيَوْمِ الْفَصْلِ‌ۚ‏(13)\nLE-YAWMIL FASLE.\nTo the day of decision!\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِؕ‏(14)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD AL-FASLE.\nAnd what will make thee know what the Day of Decision is?\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(15)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers\nاَلَمْ نُهْلِكِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nALAM NUHLEKE AWWALEEN.\nWhat! Destroyed We not the former people?\nثُمَّ نُتْبِعُهُمُ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ‏(17)\nSUMMA NUTBEU’UHUMU AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nThen did We make the later people follow them\nكَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(18)\nKAZAALEKA NAFA’ALU BE-MUJREMEEN.\nThus, We deal with the guilty ones\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(19)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers\nاَلَمْ نَخْلُقْكُّمْ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ مَّهِيْنٍۙ‏(20)\nALAM NAKHLUQKKUM MIN MAAA-IN MMAHEENIN.\nDid We not create you from a fluid despicable?\nفَجَعَلْنٰهُ فِىْ قَرَارٍ مَّكِيْنٍۙ‏(21)\nFA-JA-A’LNAAHO FEE QARAARIN MMAKEENIN.\nThen We placed it in a safe place\nاِلٰى قَدَرٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍۙ‏(22)\nELAA QADARIN MA’LOOM.\nTill the term appointed\nفَقَدَرْنَاۖ فَنِعْمَ الْقٰدِرُوْنَ‏(23)\nFAQADARNAA FA NE’MA AL-QAADEROONA.\nSo We planned then how Excellent are (We) the planners\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(24)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers!\nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ الْاَرْضَ كِفَاتًا ۙ‏(25)\nALAM NAJ-A’LIL ARZA KEFAATAN.\nHave We not made the earth a receptacle?\nاَحْيَآءً وَّاَمْوَاتًا ۙ‏(26)\nAAHYAAAN WWAAMWAATAN.\nFor the living and (also for) the dead ones\nوَّجَعَلْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ شٰمِخٰتٍ وَّ اَسْقَيْنٰكُمْ مَّآءً فُرَاتًا ؕ‏(27)\nWA JA-A’LNAA FEEHAA JA-A’LA SHAAMEKHAATIN WA AASQAYNAAKUM MMAAAN FURAATAN.\nAnd made We therein mountains high, and given you to drink water sweet?\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(28)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers!\nاِنْطَلِقُوْۤا اِلٰى مَا كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(29)\nAENTALEQOOA ELAA MAA KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\nBegone ye unto that which ye belied!\nاِنْطَلِقُوْۤا اِلٰى ظِلٍّ ذِىْ ثَلٰثِ شُعَبٍۙ‏(30)\nAENTALEQOOA ELAA ZELLIN ZEE SALAASE SHUA’ABIN.\nBegone ye unto the shadow having three columns\nلَّا ظَلِيْلٍ وَّلَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ اللَّهَبِؕ‏(31)\nLAA ZALEELIN WA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL AL-LAHABE.\n(Which yieldeth) no shade (for coolness) nor availing against the flames\nاِنَّهَا تَرْمِىْ بِشَرَرٍ كَالْقَصْرِ‌ۚ‏(32)\nINNAHAA TARMEAA BESHARARIN KAALQASRE.\nVerily, it sendeth up sparks like a palace\nكَاَنَّهٗ جِمٰلَتٌ صُفْرٌ ؕ‏(33)\nKA-ANNAHU JEMAALATUN SUFRUN.\nAs if they are tawny camels\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(34)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers!\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ لَا يَنْطِقُوْنَۙ‏(35)\nHAAZAA YAWMUD LAA YANTEQOON.\nThis is the day when they shall speak not\nوَلَا يُؤْذَنُ لَهُمْ فَيَعْتَذِرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA LAA YUZANU LAHUM FAYAA’TAZEROONA.\nAnd it shall not be permitted unto them so that they may offer excuses\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(37)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ‌ۚ جَمَعْنٰكُمْ وَالْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(38)\nHAAZAA YAWMUD FASLE JAMAA’NAAKUM WA AWWALEEN.\nThis is the Day of decision; We will gather you and (all) those of yore\nفَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ كَيْدٌ فَكِيْدُوْنِ‏(39)\nFA-IN KAANA LAKUM KAYDUN FAKEEDOONE.\nIf ye have any device, try ye that device (now)!\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(40)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers!\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ ظِلٰلٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(41)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE ZELAALIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nVerily the pious ones shall be amid shades and springs\nوَّفَوَاكِهَ مِمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nWWAFAWAAKEHA MIMMAA YASHTAHOON.\nAnd fruits whatsoever they may desire\nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِيْٓئًا ۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEEAN BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n(Unto them will be said)’. “Eat ye and drink ye in health and delight, as meed for what ye used to do\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(44)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nVerily, thus We recompense the doers of good\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(45)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers\nكُلُوْا وَتَمَتَّعُوْا قَلِيْلًا اِنَّكُمْ مُّجْرِمُوْنَ‏(46)\nKOLOO WATAMATTAU’OOA QALEELAA INNAKUM MUJREMOON.\nEat ye and enjoy yourselves a little, for verily ye are the guilty ones\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(47)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on the Day unto the beliers!\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ ارْكَعُوْا لَا يَرْكَعُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUL ARKAU’OOA LAA YARKAU’OONA.\nAnd when it is said unto them “Bow ye down!” they bow not down\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(49)\nWAYLUL YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on that Day unto the beliers!\nفَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَهٗ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(50)\nFABE-AYYE HADEESIN BAA’DAH YOAMENOONA.\nIn what other word after this will they believe?",
  "merits": "Surah al-Mursalaat (The Emissaries)\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 50 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will not be counted from the polytheists. He will always be victorious over his enemy.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that drinking this Surah after it is written, and then dissolved in water that is mixed with the water from an onion, acts as a cure from aches and pains. Keeping this Surah, written on deerskin, as a talisman, enables one to reduce the amount of time he sleeps and he will be able to stay awake for a longer time."
}
